    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/executive-assistant-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Executive Assistant - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Executive Assistant Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Administration HEO6 Continuing - Full-time HEO6 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in College Services - Science within College of Science at the City East Campus Full-time, continuing position HEO6 $94,269 - $101,828 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Provide proactive high-level executive support that enables senior leaders to focus on strategic priorities and drive outcomes across education, research and engagement. Through effective coordination, communication and stakeholder management, you will help advance the College of Science's contribution to the University and wider community. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Senior Executive Officer, you will join the College Executive Services team within the College of Science. Working closely with the Pro Vice Chancellor, Executive Director and key stakeholders, your ability to anticipate requirements and coordinate key activities will help enable the effective operation of the College. Visit the AU website to learn more about the College of Science. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working in a fast-paced, collaborative environment where priorities can shift quickly. You will be part of a supportive team that values initiative, professionalism and strong relationships, with opportunities to engage with a diverse range of colleagues and external partners. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience providing high-level executive or administrative support to a senior executive in a complex organisation Experience managing diaries, meetings, travel and events for senior leaders Strong organisational and time management skills, with attention to detail Proficiency in drafting and editing correspondence, reports and presentations Experience maintaining confidential records, handling sensitive matters with discretion and professionalism and using digital information systems Experience supporting financial processes and procurement Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build relationships across diverse teams Ability to work independently, prioritise competing demands and adapt to changing circumstances Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us about your key relevant experience and why you’re excited about the role Submit your application by 11:30 pm Tuesday, 15 September 2026. The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493365): Rachael Cossons Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
