    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/senior-organisational-performance-specialist-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Organisational Performance Specialist",
      "description": "Senior Organisational Performance Specialist - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Senior Organisational Performance Specialist Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Human resources Continuing - Full-time HEO8 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the People and Culture Portfolio located in Adelaide CBD Full-time, continuing position Salary Range: $116,320 - $130,498 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The Senior Organisational Performance specialist leads and delivers organisational development initiatives that strengthen organisational performance, capability and culture, enhance leadership practice, and support sustainable organisational change. Working closely with leaders and stakeholders across the University, you will design and implement evidence-based programs, facilitate team development initiatives, oversee coaching and mentoring opportunities, and provide expert insights that strengthen individual, team and organisational effectiveness. As a trusted advisor, you will translate organisational development strategies into practical solutions for leaders and teams, informed by workforce data, insights and diagnostics. You will contribute to reporting, business case development, and the continuous enhancement of frameworks and resources that enable organisational outcomes. Through collaborative partnerships and a practical, solutions-focused approach, you will drive initiatives that enhance organisational performance and strengthen workforce capability and culture across the University. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Senior Manager, Organisational Performance, this role is part of a specialist team within Organisational Capability, a strategic function responsible for shaping the employee experience and enabling organisational success. Through initiatives spanning performance, recognition, succession, leadership and culture, the team designs and delivers practical solutions that build capability, deepen engagement and create meaningful outcomes for employees, leaders and the broader University community. Visit the AU website to learn more about People and Culture Portfolio Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. If you thrive in complex environments, enjoy influencing outcomes and are motivated by meaningful work, this role offers the chance to make a lasting difference. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven ability to develop and implement organisational development strategies and initiatives, including leadership capability, organisational culture, coaching, and change support Experience using tools to measure and strengthen organisational health, including interventions at individual, team, and organisation levels Proven ability in data analysis and interpretation, with advanced skills in preparing and presenting analytical and strategic reports Experience in coaching and facilitation, with the ability to engage and influence staff and leaders at various levels Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 13 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493060): Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
