    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-b-c-x-2-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow B/C x 2",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow B/C x 2 - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Postdoctoral Research Fellow B/C x 2 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level B Level C Fixed term - Full-time Level C Add to favourites View favourites Based in the College of Engineering and Information Technology Full-time fixed term contract until 31 March 2028 Salary Range Level B: $117,100 - $138,515 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Salary Range Level C: $142,789 - $164,207 Per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters You will bring strong theoretical and practical expertise in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering or equivalent, with a relevant degree and PhD (or equivalent research experience), a track record of publications, and the ability to turn research into tangible outcomes. You’ll be a collaborative, hands-on team player, confident working with investigators and industry partners, with experience in experimentation, project delivery and, ideally, open-source reinforcement learning tools. The team Adelaide University’s School of Computer Science and Information Technology delivers industry-driven education and globally impactful research, equipping graduates & researchers with skills in artificial intelligence, cyber security, software engineering, and innovation to become impactful citizens of the digital society. Visit the AU website to learn more about the School of Computer Science and Information Technology Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This is an opportunity to join a vibrant team as we launch Australia’s new university for the future, Adelaide University. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience, for Level B : A PhD (completed or near completion) in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Performance Engineering or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research expertise in experimental computer systems, performance evaluation, benchmarking, computer architecture, embedded/HPC systems or a closely related area. Demonstrated experience designing controlled and repeatable experiments, including quantitative data analysis, statistical reasoning, validation and interpretation of results. Experience with FPGA, GPU or accelerator technologies. Familiarity with high performance or embedded computing Strong programming and data-analysis capability, preferably including Python and C/C++ A record of high-quality research outputs commensurate with opportunity and demonstrated ability to communicate complex technical findings clearly. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with software engineers, researchers and external stakeholders and to deliver against project milestones. Ability to work appropriately with sensitive project information and comply with applicable University and project security requirements. Australian Citizenship To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience, for Level C : A PhD (completed or near completion) in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical/Electronic Engineering, Performance Engineering or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated research expertise in experimental computer systems, performance evaluation, benchmarking, computer architecture, embedded/HPC systems or a closely related area. Demonstrated experience designing controlled and repeatable experiments, including quantitative data analysis, statistical reasoning, validation and interpretation of results. Experience with systems profiling and measurement tools and with metrics such as latency, throughput, utilisation, memory bandwidth, power consumption and thermal behaviour. Knowledge of heterogeneous computing and one or more of CPUs, GPUs, FPGAs, SoCs/MPSoCs or specialised accelerators is highly desirable. Experience evaluating CPUs, GPUs, FPGAs, SoCs, DSPs or related computing platforms. Strong programming and data-analysis capability, preferably including Python and C/C++, A record of high-quality research outputs commensurate with opportunity and demonstrated ability to communicate complex technical findings clearly. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with and manage a small team of software engineers, researchers and external stakeholders and to deliver against project milestones. Ability to work appropriately with sensitive project information and comply with applicable University and project security requirements. Australian Citizenship Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role upload a document that includes your responses to all the experience criteria Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 27 Sep 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493428 ). Evelyn Ruth Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications are welcomed from Australian citizens, residing in Australia only. Appointment is subject to a Personnel Security Clearance at NEGATIVE VETTING LEVEL 1 being obtained and maintained. #LI-DNI Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
