    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/data-engineer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Data Engineer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Data Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Engineering HEO7 Fixed term - Full-time HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Business Intelligence team at the City West campus Full-time 24 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Ensure the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Enable data-driven decision-making by designing, developing, and maintaining robust data pipelines, models, and solutions that support the Adelaide University’s strategic and operational objectives. The role ensures the integrity, accessibility, and quality of data assets to empower business intelligence and analytics across the institution. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Business Intelligence team within the Performance, Data and Insights Function and is aligned to the Corporate Portfolio within the University. The Data Engineer will work most closely with the Chief Data and Analytics Officer, Director, Business Intelligence, and the IT and Finance teams. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Corporate Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in data manipulation, preparation, and integration Experience in designing, developing, and supporting data pipelines, models, and processes Proficiency in data management and business intelligence concepts and practices Experience with data manipulation tools and/or programming languages such as Power Query, Alteryx, SQL, and R Experience in stakeholder engagement, expectations, and relationship management Advanced Microsoft Office skills Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 13 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493457): Alexandra Koszegi Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/teaching-casuals-au-online-2026-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026",
      "description": "Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026 - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Teaching Casuals (AU Online) – 2026 Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Casual Campaign Casual Casual rates apply Add to favourites View favourites At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Do you have a passion for online teaching? Are you interested in supporting students who want to study on demand, and do you possess specialist knowledge and skills to teach in the fields of: Business & Law Creative Arts, Design and Humanities Education, Behavioural and Social Sciences Engineering and Information Technology Health and/or Science? With degrees spanning a wide range of programs, Adelaide University Online is accepting expressions of interest for casual teaching academics who are interested in undertaking sessional teaching contracts. About Adelaide University Online Adelaide University Online (AUO) offers a range of 100% online degrees and aspires to be the best online education provider in Australia. Our programs are delivered across two distinct models: 10-week periods delivered over 4 terms per year 6-week periods delivered over 6 terms per year Targeted at busy adults who need to juggle work, life and family commitments, AUO is making it possible for more people to integrate study into their busy lives and pursue their career goals. Each degree has been specifically designed for online learning and is delivered in an engaging and flexible way. Students can access academics and study support out of hours and on weekends, so they can get help when they need it. Application Process: Please view the available courses through the application form, to determine what area of work offerings are being made available for individual. Ensure you meet the essential criteria – essential skills and experience listed below. Note: This is a fully remote, flexible role with work conducted primarily outside standard Monday to Friday, 9am-5pm office hours. Core Responsibilities Undertake online teaching as part of the AUO teaching team Apply disciplinary expertise to consult, facilitate discussions, mark assessment items, and provide feedback to students Implement approaches that maximise the student experience and learning outcomes Provide academic support, mentoring and advice to students Act as the first point of response/contact in managing student issues or complaints Essential Skills and Experience Minimum Bachelor’s degree and relevant professional/industry work experience (10-week courses) Minimum Masters or PhD (6-week courses) Ability to undertake a range of teaching duties in an online environment Ability to actively engage and educate a diverse student group Excellent written and interpersonal skills Ability to use the necessary digital techniques and tools required for effective online teaching Available to work outside of normal working hours, including weekends Please contact Academic and Program Services at auoacademic.programservices@adelaide.edu.au if you have any questions about this process. Please note, this email is for enquiries only. Applications will only be accepted through the online portal. Please note - By registering on the Casual/Sessional Staff Register, it does not guarantee that employment will be offered. If you already hold a casual contract with Adelaide University, please apply and complete the application form to be considered for future opportunities. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia and for the term of appointment. To be eligible, you will need to reside within Australia. Submit your application by 11:30pm Friday 18 September 2026 Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. #S-DNI #LI-DN Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/school-of-nursing-and-midwifery-teaching-casuals-tutors-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "School of Nursing and Midwifery Teaching casuals (tutors)",
      "description": "School of Nursing and Midwifery Teaching casuals (tutors) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me School of Nursing and Midwifery Teaching casuals (tutors) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Casual Campaign Education & Training Healthcare & Medical Casual Casual rates apply Add to favourites View favourites The position is primarily focussed on the delivery of courses within the school’s undergraduate and postgraduate nursing or midwifery programs. You will work with guidance and direction from course coordinators.  The role of tutor utilises contemporary professional/discipline-related knowledge in their teaching practice and carries out activities to develop scholarly expertise. Core Responsibilities: Under direction conduct learning activities including lectures, tutorials, assessment and provide timely feedback to students. Use a variety of pedagogical techniques (including face-to-face, online and blended learning) to foster student learning. Undertake high quality teaching as part of the teaching team, including participation in moderation of marking exercises. Incorporate contemporary professional/discipline-based knowledge in teaching activities Act as a student advisor by responding promptly to queries and directing students to appropriate supports/services. Undertake administrative functions connected to courses taught. Actively participate in meetings and committees at the discipline, program and Academic Unit level. Experience Required: Relevant and recent clinical experience. High level written and oral communication skills including the ability to effectively collaborate with team members, combined with cultural sensitivity. Demonstrated ability to actively engage and educate a student group. Be capable of using the necessary digital technologies required for effective curriculum delivery. High level administrative and organisational skills. Eligibility Requirements: Bachelor of Nursing or Bachelor of Midwifery and relevant postgraduate qualification in a nursing or midwifery specialisation together with current registration, or eligibility for registration, with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia including a current practicing certificate as a Registered Nurse or Midwife. If you have any questions about the process, please contact Dean.SNM@adelaide.edu.au Please note – By registering on the Casual/Sessional Staff Register, it does not guarantee that employment will be offered. If you already hold a casual contract with Adelaide University, please complete the application form to be considered for future opportunities. Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #S-DNI #LI-DNI Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/emergency-and-critical-care-veterinarian-casual-opportunities-roseworthy-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Together, we will defineAdelaide University",
      "description": "Emergency and Critical Care Veterinarian - Casual Opportunities - Roseworthy, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Emergency and Critical Care Veterinarian - Casual Opportunities Roseworthy, SA, Australia, 5371 HEO7 Casual HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Based at Roseworthy Campus, University of Adelaide Casual role, various shifts available on a 24/7 roster (HEO 7) $64.33 to $74.46 per hour plus an employer contribution of 12% superannuation applies. In addition, loadings between 15% and 40% apply when working outside the normal span of hours in accordance with the University of Adelaide Enterprise Agreement . At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As a member of the Emergency and Critical Care (ECC) team at the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital, you will provide high-quality care to a varied and growing caseload of small animal patients through a 24/7 roster. You will have access to advanced imaging modalities, including CT, and work closely with a dedicated radiographer and onsite veterinary diagnostic laboratory, enabling collaboration with pathologists to achieve the best patient outcomes. As part of the Roseworthy Veterinary Hospital team, you will provide high-quality emergency and critical care for small animals while contributing to the clinical education of future veterinarians. Your work will directly impact patient outcomes, student learning, and the ongoing development of a vibrant teaching hospital. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team You will join a motivated and experienced team of veterinarians, nurses, and support staff delivering emergency and critical care services 24/7. Reporting to the Head of Emergency and Critical Care, your role will contribute to both patient care and veterinary education. Supported by a team of experienced academic specialists, you will engage in daily case discussions and contribute to complex clinical decision-making. In addition, you will play a key role in the education of final-year veterinary students, involving them in case management and providing hands-on learning opportunities while modeling the highest standards of clinical and professional practice, helping to shape the next generation of veterinarians. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Veterinary Health Centre: https://www.adelaide.edu.au/vet/ Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity, and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation, and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys a dynamic and varied clinical environment, working with a wide range of patients, colleagues, and final-year students, keeping each workday engaging and rewarding. Learn more about our people, what we stand for, and what we offer at Careers at AU. Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Veterinary qualification with eligibility to be registered in South Australia Experience in first-opinion or emergency services, including emergency surgery Strong communication and interpersonal skills with clients and team members Enthusiasm and experience in assisting, teaching, or mentoring others High-level written communication skills, including medical records, referral letters, and client correspondence Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, supporting flexible working arrangements and reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: Your current CV A cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role This will remain open until all roles filled The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact: Simone Patterson Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Software Engineer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Computer Science and Information Technology Join a high-impact research project at the forefront of next-generation computing technology. Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) Waite (Urrbrae), SA, Australia, 5064 School of Agriculture, Food and Wine Opportunity for a Research Fellow – Plasma Seed Enhancement (B) to join the School of Agriculture, Food and Wine to research and scale up a new technology - Plasma Seed Enhancement (PSE). Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 School of Psychology Shape the next generation of psychologists through teaching, research and professional practice, with opportunities to contribute expertise in health or organisational psychology. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/grant-funded-researcher-b-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-4eeb3c1d-d5d5-4e67-845d-cc766e25e28f": {
      "title": "Grant-Funded Researcher (B)",
      "description": "Grant-Funded Researcher (B) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Grant-Funded Researcher (B) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Level B Science & Technology Fixed term - Full-time Level B Add to favourites View favourites Based in the School of Computer Science and Information Technology Full-time fixed-term, 36-month opportunity within a leading research environment Salary range: Level B, $117,100 - $138,515 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Opportunity to supervise emerging researchers and HDR students At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As a Research Fellow (Level B), you will contribute to the advancement of knowledge through high-quality research and the development of innovative solutions to real-world problems. Your work will support meaningful outcomes for industry, government and the broader community, while strengthening Adelaide University's growing research profile. Curious to learn more? Explore the information below to discover more about this opportunity. The team You will join a collaborative and forward-thinking research environment within the School of Computer Science and Information Technology. Working alongside leading researchers, industry partners and students, you will contribute to projects that deliver impactful outcomes across a range of contemporary challenges. To know more about the School of Computer Science and Information Technology, click here! Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who enjoys working in a dynamic and collaborative research environment, engaging with diverse stakeholders and contributing to projects that create tangible impact. You will have the opportunity to work across interdisciplinary teams, build meaningful partnerships and help shape future research directions. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU. Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Qualifications A PhD in a relevant discipline or equivalent accreditation and standing appropriate to a Level B Research academic appointment. Essential Selection Criteria Significant experience in undertaking basic research and/or applied research and development (R&D). Established track record in delivering solutions to real-world problems through software development, mathematical formulation, experimentation and/or statistical analysis. Significant experience in the management of research and/or applied R&D projects and programs. Demonstrated ability to engage and collaborate effectively with external partners on shared initiatives and projects. Evidence of professional contributions, including activities such as organising workshops, conferences, symposia or similar events. Demonstrated commitment to the organisational values of integrity, respect, collegiality, excellence and discovery, and the ability to positively uphold associated behavioural expectations. Desirable Experience supervising junior researchers and/or Higher Degree by Research (HDR) students to achieve research outcomes, including publications and theses. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you will need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm 23 September 2026. Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact ( quoting reference number 493461 ): Amra Delibasic Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/triage-counsellor-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Triage Counsellor",
      "description": "Triage Counsellor - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Continuing - Part-time HEO8 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Student Experience and Success Portfolio based at the City East campus Part-time (0.6 FTE), continuing role Salary Range: $116,320 - $130,498 (pro-rated) per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters This role will report to the Senior Manager, Student Wellbeing and Safety. This role forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team The Student Experience and Success (SES) Portfolio plays a key role in providing a connected, inclusive, and transformative experience for every student, ensuring they feel supported, engaged, and confident as they navigate university life and prepare for their future. Visit the AU website to learn more about the Student Experience and Success portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience as a counsellor and/or mental health clinician, with evidence of high- level competence in delivering services and supporting individuals with mental health conditions and/or crisis Demonstrated experience providing intake and assessment services, including triage and crisis interventions, to a diverse client group Highly developed interpersonal, communication, and negotiation skills, including the ability to work effectively with people from a wide range of educational, social, and cultural backgrounds Eligibility to register with the Psychology Board of Australia through the Australian Health Regulation Agency (AHPRA) and/or the Australian Association of Social Workers (AASW) is also required Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re suitable for the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 27 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493473) Suzanah Saha Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold a current Working with Children Check. Appointment is subject to a satisfactory National Police Check (NPC) being obtained and maintained. #LI-DNI #S-DN I Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 0a6b0714 Last Name (required) 18ed74c5 Email (required) 3e567a35 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 05aeaac5 Last Name (required) 562697d7 Email (required) 7320a171 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Remediation Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead the resolution of complex pay discrepancies, overseeing remediation activi