    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/team-lead-quality-and-compliance-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Team Lead, Quality and Compliance",
      "description": "Team Lead, Quality and Compliance - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO7 Fixed term - Full-time HEO7 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in People & Culture at the City West Campus Two (2) Full-time, 12-month fixed term contract opportunities Salary Range: $103,719 - $116,002 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Help shape a culture of integrity, accountability and excellence at Adelaide University. In this influential leadership role, you'll lead and empower a high-performing Quality and Compliance team, partnering with stakeholders across the University to strengthen People and Culture practices, enhance governance frameworks and drive continuous improvement. You'll play a critical role in delivering audit readiness, embedding effective controls and building organisational capability to support trusted, compliant and high-performing people services. Through your expertise and leadership, you'll enable meaningful change that helps our people thrive and supports Adelaide University's strategic ambitions and long-term success. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team As part of the Quality and Compliance team, you'll work alongside dedicated professionals focused on strengthening governance, compliance, payroll integrity and continuous improvement.  Together, the team helps ensure People and Culture services are trusted, compliant and responsive to the needs of a dynamic university environment, enabling staff and the institution to succeed. Working closely with People Services and Careers, Legal, Risk, data and analytics teams, senior leaders, and external regulatory bodies, the team provides trusted advice on complex compliance matters, support audit activities, monitor legislative changes, and helps embed consistent, compliant practices across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about People & Culture. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. The ideal candidate for this role is an experienced people leader with a strong background in quality, compliance, audit or risk management within a complex organisational environment.  You will bring the proven ability to lead and develop high-performing teams, build trusted relationships across diverse stakeholders and drive a culture of accountability, continuous improvement and service excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven experience leading and developing teams, including managing workload, building capability and driving consistent performance outcomes Demonstrated experience in quality, compliance, risk or audit functions, including designing, implementing and testing controls and audit activities Experience developing and applying compliance frameworks and governance processes within complex organisational environments Proven ability to analyse compliance risks, provide practical advice and leading the implementation of effective mitigation strategies Experience in managing audit processes, including planning, evidence collection, coordination of responses and tracking of issues and actions Proven experience in and/or understanding of process improvement methodology Excellent written communication and stakeholder management skills, including the ability to influence outcomes and support effective collaboration across stakeholders Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30p m Sunday 27 September 2027 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493508 ) : Emma Kelvin , Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 2a651b15 Last Name (required) 9060f228 Email (required) c7d714a6 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 3e77d1e9 Last Name (required) fbe96e6b Email (required) 4de5159f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Remediation Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead the resolution of complex pay discrepancies, overseeing remediation activities that deliver accurate employee entitlements and strengthen compliance outcomes across the University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 4f36d4e1 Last Name (required) e3bf9966 Email (required) 4d4f6b48 Job Alert 86f102cb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO7 HEO7 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
