    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/technical-research-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Technical Research Officer",
      "description": "Technical Research Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO5 Science & Technology Fixed term - Full-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in College of Engineering and Information Technology in the Adelaide CBD Full-time, fixed-term position for 12 months HEO5, $84,498 - $93,955 per annum plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities that contribute to the Centre for Automotive Safety Research's at-scene crash investigation program, vehicle testing operations and associated research initiatives. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Research - Engineering and Information Technology team within the College of Engineering and Information Technology and is aligned to the Provost Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about College of Engineering and Information Technology Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven ability to contribute to research, testing or data collection activities as part of a multidisciplinary team Proven ability to communicate effectively with a range of stakeholders, including researchers, students and external organisations Proven ability to organise competing priorities and maintain attention to detail in a technical or research environment Experience supporting research, laboratory, testing or technical operations activities Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Sunday 27 September 2026. The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493399): Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold a current Working with Children Check. Appointment is subject to a satisfactory National Police Check (NPC) being obtained and maintained. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 09985c87 Last Name (required) 58bc9965 Email (required) 61ce039c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) fa46f5e4 Last Name (required) c347d52c Email (required) b5ae7033 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Remediation Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Lead the resolution of complex pay discrepancies, overseeing remediation activities that deliver accurate employee entitlements and strengthen compliance outcomes