    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/knowledge-and-compliance-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Knowledge and Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Knowledge and Compliance Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO6 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time HEO6 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Quality and Compliance team in People & Culture at City West Full-time 12 month fixed term contract Salary Range: $94,269 - $101,828 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As the Knowledge and Compliance Officer, you will support Colleges and Portfolios to embed consistent and compliant pay and entitlement practices across Adelaide University. Reporting to the Change Specialist, you will deliver local education, training and awareness activities, provide guidance to managers and staff, and support the adoption of compliant practices. You will maintain accurate and accessible knowledge resources, including guidance materials, FAQs and knowledge articles, manage and triage enquiries, and escalate matters to subject matter experts where required. You will also support compliance tracking, reporting and document governance to monitor training, engagement and ongoing compliance. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of the Change and Education Stream within the Pay Accuracy and Entitlement Program and is aligned to the People and Culture Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about People and Culture . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who is an excellent communicator who is organised, detail-focused and confident working with stakeholders. You will have experience in administration, learning support, compliance or knowledge management, and the ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines and handle sensitive information appropriately. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: In administration, learning support, compliance coordination or knowledge management Delivering training and education activities and evaluating their effectiveness through learner engagement and knowledge transfer measures Managing multiple initiatives and delivering outcomes within established timeframes. Proven ability to apply strong attention to detail and manage documentation accurately Use of Microsoft 365 tools to support coordination, tracking and reporting activities. Proven ability to handle sensitive information appropriately and work to deadlines Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter the online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Wednesday 30 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493509 ) : Emma Kelvin Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 82224759 Last Name (required) 1ca13eec Email (required) 4ffd00f5 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) bc894ad2 Last Name (required) 6b86605c Email (required) fe6125bc Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Remediation Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia,