    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/remediation-lead-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Remediation Lead",
      "description": "Remediation Lead - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Remediation Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO8 Fixed term - Full-time HEO8 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Pay Accuracy and Entitlements Program at the City West campus Full-time, fixed term contract until 31 July 2028 Salary Range: $116,320 - $130,498 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Lead a critical program of work that makes a real difference to our people. As Remediation Lead, you will oversee the end-to-end delivery of pay remediation activities across Adelaide University, ensuring employees receive the correct entitlements through fair, accurate and compliant processes. Leading a specialist team, you will establish robust methodologies, quality controls and governance practices while identifying opportunities to improve systems, processes and compliance outcomes. Your expertise will help shape sustainable solutions that enhance pay accuracy into the future. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team Join a team delivering meaningful outcomes for our people. In this role, you will partner with payroll, employee relations, legal and business leaders to navigate complex remediation matters, provide clear and practical advice, manage escalations, and contribute to lasting improvements in pay accuracy, governance and employee experience Visit the AU website to learn more about the People and Culture Portfolio . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who is an experienced payroll, HR, compliance or remediation professional with strong analytical, stakeholder and leadership skills. You will be confident navigating complex frameworks, analysing data, managing sensitive matters and driving continuous improvement. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Proven experience in leading teams or workflows delivering payroll remediation, payroll operations, human resources compliance or audit activities in complex environments. Excellent interpersonal and negotiation skills, enabling effective interaction with stakeholders and collaborators to provide advice, guide decision-making, and secure cooperation and engagement in remediation delivery. Demonstrated ability to provide strategic advice, analysis and evaluation for identifying and managing remediation projects. Proven ability to interpret and apply legal advice, industrial instruments, pay rules or equivalent regulated frameworks. Proven ability to apply strong data literacy and attention to detail to analyse and validate payroll data and calculations, and identify causation or non-compliance. Proven ability to manage sensitive matters, including stakeholder escalations and compliance-related issues, and drive continuous improvement through root-cause analysis and control uplift. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11: 30pm Sunday 27 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493478 ): Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 833cb730 Last Name (required) 5822b24e Email (required) cde458e9 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 51c00464 Last Name (required) f0e95243 Email (required) 5b0b6841 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 32f7f956 Last Name (required) a89bbe42 Email (required) f10df8f6 Job Alert d8de8a58 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO8 HEO8 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
