    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/credit-and-admissions-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-df2ff528-484b-43d6-81ad-8e6f47f610f4": {
      "title": "Credit and Admissions Officer",
      "description": "Credit and Admissions Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Credit and Admissions Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO5 Continuing - Full-time Fixed term - Full-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in Student Engagement and Success Portfolio at multiple Adelaide metropolitan Campuses. 2 Full-time, continuing positions 1 Fixed-term contract for 8months 1 Fixed-term contract for 12 months HEO5, $84,498 - $93,955 per annum plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As a Credit and Admissions Officer, you will help to ensure internal transfer and credit assessments are accurately completed following relevant approval processes. You will also provide timely and consistent communications with stakeholders across the University, to ensure equitable, efficient outcomes for students and applicants. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to a Team Lead, Credit and Admissions, these roles form part of the Scholarships and Admissions Standards team within the Student and Academic Services Function. You will work closely with internal support service areas, students, as well as both academic and professional staff across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about Student Engagement and Success . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is suited for individuals who prefer a degree of predictability in their work. This role will involve consistent tasks and regular interactions with familiar colleagues. You will be able to develop strong working relationships with your colleagues and contribute to a stable and reliable team, perfect for candidates who excel in providing exceptional service and support to students, staff and stakeholders. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in a complex service organisation Proven ability in the provision of high-level advice and recommendations to Senior Staff Experience in research and analytical skills Experience in interpretation of policies and procedure Proven ability in advanced written and verbal communication Proven ability with attention to detail Key deliverables Joining us means you will strive for excellence in: Accurate Credit Assessments – Complete all credit assessments accurately and within agreed timelines, ensuring data integrity Timely Admissions Processing – Process admissions efficiently to meet student load targets and compliance standards Effective Stakeholder Communication – Build strong relationships and maintain clear communication with stakeholders Data Integrity and Compliance – Ensure all credit agreement applications comply with University standards and legislative requirements Strategic Policy Development – Assist in developing and implementing policies that align with University goals Continuous Improvement Initiatives – Lead initiatives to improve processes and enhance service quality Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter of no more than 2 pages (1000 words maximum), which addresses the point below: Select 3 Key Deliverables of this role. Identify one of your personal strengths for each Key Deliverable and describe how it aligns. Submit your application by 11:30pm Thursday 24 September 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493474) : Taryn Giles Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #S-DNI #LI-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) d47307a8 Last Name (required) af4ad640 Email (required) 7ecfd23f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 24a0b4c9 Last Name (required) 4c09d2f7 Email (required) b9b66e11 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5a5e941d Last Name (required) 21f9105b Email (required) 3c5d3045 Job Alert ef112247 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO5 HEO5 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio Student Experience and Success Student Experience and Success Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn 