    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/credit-and-admissions-services-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Credit and Admissions Services Officer",
      "description": "Credit and Admissions Services Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Credit and Admissions Services Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Administration HEO4 Continuing - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in Student Engagement and Success Portfolio at the Adelaide City Campus Full-time, continuing position available Salary Range (HEO 4): $75,366 – $82,607 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As a Credit and Admissions Services Officer, you will help to ensure internal transfer and credit assessments are accurately completed following relevant approval processes. You will also provide timely and consistent communications with stakeholders across the University, to ensure equitable, efficient outcomes for students and applicants. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to a Team Lead, Credit and Admissions, this role forms part of Scholarships and Admissions Standards team within the Student and Academic Services Function. You will work closely with internal support service areas, students as well as both academic and professional staff across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about Student Engagement and Success . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is suited for individuals who prefer a degree of predictability in their work. This role will involve consistent tasks and regular interactions with familiar colleagues. You will be able to develop strong working relationships with your colleagues and contribute to a stable and reliable team. Perfect for candidates who excel in providing exceptional service and support to students, staff and stakeholders. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in complex service organisation Proven ability in the provision of high-level advice and recommendations Experience in research and analytical skills Experience in interpretation of policies and procedures Proven ability in written and verbal communication Proven ability with attention to detail Key deliverables Joining us means you will strive for excellence in: Accurate Credit Assessments – Ensure all domestic and international credit assessments are completed accurately and within specified timelines Effective Stakeholder Communication – Maintain clear and consistent communication with internal and external stakeholders Timely Admissions Processing – Process admissions promptly to meet student load targets and compliance requirements Continuous Improvement Initiatives – Contribute to improvements in credit and admissions processes to enhance efficiency and service quality Successful System Implementation – Support the implementation of new or revised systems through training and communication Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter of no more than 2 pages (1000 words maximum), which addresses the two points below: Select 2 Key Deliverables of this role. Identify one of your personal strengths for each Key Deliverable and describe how it aligns. Our work can, at times, be repetitive with bulk processing and data entry. What strategies do you use to ensure accuracy and speed in getting through large blocks of similar work? Submit your application by 11:30pm T hursday 24 September 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493468) : Taryn Giles Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 602932e2 Last Name (required) 50145bea Email (required) 22b41d5e Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 1faefe1b Last Name (required) 510a5715 Email (required) 8a89f1b3 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsell