    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/quality-and-compliance-administrator-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Quality and Compliance Administrator",
      "description": "Quality and Compliance Administrator - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Quality and Compliance Administrator Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Administration HEO4 Fixed term - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the People and Culture, Quality and Compliance team at the City West campus Two Full-time 12-month fixed term contracts Salary Range: $75,366 - $82,607 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Provide administrative and operational support to quality and compliance activities by maintaining accurate records, coordinating activities, and supporting audit and compliance processes within People and Culture. Maintain record management systems, registers and documentation to ensure accurate, current and accessible records across Adelaide University, and coordinate audit activities and scheduling to support timely delivery of audit and compliance requirements. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Quality and Compliance team within the People Services and Careers Function and is aligned to the People and Culture Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the People and Culture portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience in administrative or support roles Proven ability to apply strong organisational skills and attention to detail Proven ability to manage routine tasks and follow instructions effectively Experience using systems and handling data to support administrative and coordination activities Proven ability to communicate effectively and support team activities Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter, no more than two pages, demonstrating your transferrable skills and experience for the role. Submit your application by 11:30pm Wednesday 23 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493500 ) : Emma Kelvin, Consultant, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) e2ac580d Last Name (required) 5f0dadf7 Email (required) ce35a4dd Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) d6af2350 Last Name (required) 6d1e362d Email (required) 0ee4167a Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) b4184554 Last Name (required) 7f30ee0b Email (required) 2ec42a9b Job Alert 5209b106 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration HEO4 Administration HEO4 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People