    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-level-b-and-senior-lecturer-level-c-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Lecturer (Level B) and Senior Lecturer (Level C) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level B Level C Continuing - Full-time Level C Add to favourites View favourites Based in the College of Education, Behavioural and Social Sciences at Adelaide City Campus Full-time, continuing positions Salary: $114,917 - $135,932 (Level B) or starting at $140,127 (Level C) plus 17% superannuation Work in a collaborative, passionate team alongside world-class researchers At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters The School of Psychology invites applications for a Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in Psychology , with expertise in health psychology or organisational psychology . Appointment will be made at Level B or Level C, commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications, experience and academic track record. In this role, you will contribute to the education and development of future psychology professionals through high-quality teaching, supervision, mentoring, research and professional practice. You will help create engaging learning experiences, strengthen the School’s research and professional activities and contribute to a collaborative academic community. At Senior Lecturer level , you will also provide academic leadership across teaching, research and professional practice, mentor colleagues and contribute to the ongoing development of capability within the School. The team The Lecturer / Senior Lecturer will join the School of Psychology within the College of Education, Behavioural and Social Sciences and will report to Professor Peter Strelan, Dean of the School of Psychology . You will work alongside leading researchers, educators and practitioners within a collaborative academic environment, with opportunities to contribute to organisational and human factors psychology and build connections across disciplines, professional practice and industry. Visit the AU website to learn more about the School of Psychology. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This opportunity is ideal for someone who is passionate about psychology education, research and professional practice and wants to contribute to the development of the next generation of psychology professionals. You will join a warm, collegial and supportive academic environment, working alongside leading researchers, educators and practitioners with opportunities to build collaborations and further develop your own academic and professional profile. For appointment at Senior Lecturer level , you will also have the opportunity to mentor and support colleagues, contribute to the development of teaching and research capability and help shape the future direction of psychology within the School. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Lecturer Level B: A Masters degree or equivalent in Psychology Registration as a Psychologist in Australia, with Endorsement in Health or Organisational Psychology, or the ability and willingness to gain Endorsement. Board Approved Supervisor with the Psychology Board of Australia, or the ability and willingness to gain supervisor status. Demonstrated experience of placement supervision Clearly defined research interests aligned with the School’s research strengths. A developing record of quality peer-reviewed publications, relative to opportunity. Ability to supervise the research of undergraduate, honours or postgraduate students, relative to opportunity. Knowledge of modern teaching pedagogy (e.g., flipped classrooms, simulation) and authentic assessment practices and demonstrated ability and willingness to implement them. Demonstrated ability to be adaptable to a changing education environment including online teaching. Excellent communication and organisational skills. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the Adelaide University’s values. Desirable Criteria 12. A PhD in the area of Organisational Psychology or Health Psychology or the willingness to enrol in a PhD Senior Lecturer Level C A doctoral qualification in Psychological Science or in a related field Experience in program co-ordination Experience taking significant roles in research projects including, where appropriate, leadership of a research team; Demonstrated record of the development and delivery of excellent teaching and learning experiences in a range of settings and student experience levels. Experience in postgraduate supervision, and a history of success in completion of doctoral and master’s candidates. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter Please ensure your application includes a separate document addressing each of the selection criteria outlined in the Role Experience section of the job advertisement. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 5 October 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact ( quoting job reference 493351) Georgia Borg Recruitment Consultant +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
