      "title": "Technical Officer",
      "description": "Technical Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Technical Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO5 Continuing - Part-time HEO5 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based within the College of Health, in the City West Campus Part-time (0.8FTE), continuing position $84,498 - $93,955 per annum (pro rata) plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Deliver specialised technical support and exercise operational judgement to manage complex research requirements at Adelaide University. Support research laboratories, centres and institutes by applying advanced technical expertise, independently preparing and processing research materials, maintaining specialised equipment, resolving technical issues and contributing to laboratory standards and improvement. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Specialist Facilities and Technical Services team within the College of Health Function and is aligned to the Provost Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about College of Health . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience delivering specialised technical support for complex research activities Experience independently preparing and processing research materials, samples or reagents Experience operating, maintaining and troubleshooting complex laboratory equipment Experience applying technical judgement to resolve non‑routine laboratory issues Experience advising researchers and research students on laboratory methods and equipment use Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 29 September 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493437) : Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #S-DNI #LI-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 55a38b43 Last Name (required) b2ff8ea2 Email (required) 5de0b118 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 8fb21980 Last Name (required) 2b0c743c Email (required) a3d15f17 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 9bf88486 Last Name (required) 47f3d8e0 Email (required) 3f4af8ba Job Alert cb4563e0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO5 HEO5 Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Health College of Health Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
