    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-research-fellow-a-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow (A)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow (A) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Postdoctoral Research Fellow (A) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Level A Fixed term - Full-time Level A Add to favourites View favourites Based in the Faculty of health, SAiGENCI 12 Months Fixed Term contract (1 FTE) extendable for further 2 years Level A - $103,962 - $111,384 per annum plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Research Fellow in computational and systems biology to lead the mechanistic modelling stream of a new research program on adaptive resistance to targeted cancer therapy. The successful candidate will develop and calibrate mechanism models that link time-resolved signalling adaptation to drug exposure (PK), target and pathway modulation (PD), and tumour dynamics, with EGFR- and KRAS-driven non-small cell lung cancer as the flagship setting. A complementary stream applying machine learning to pharmacogenomic and patient-derived datasets to build deployable predictive biomarker panels offers additional scope. Work that matters The Integrative Network Modelling Group within the Computational Systems Oncology program at SAiGENCI sits at the intersection of mathematics, computation, and cancer biology. We develop mechanistic, predictive models of cellular decision-making to address both fundamental and translational challenges in oncology, including drug resistance, pathway rewiring, and the discovery of new therapeutic vulnerabilities. Beyond cancer specifically, our research explores broader questions regarding cell fate decisions, the hidden dynamics of complex signalling networks, and their underlying regulatory mechanisms. Our approach is deliberately cancer-agnostic, focusing on principles that generalize across various tumour types while exploring the governing and design principles that dictate complex signalling behaviour. A defining feature of our group is the tight integration of dynamic network modelling with experimental and clinical insight, enabling us to move beyond mere description and toward robust, actionable prediction. If you are a talented systems biologist driven by both curiosity and discipline, we want you on our team! The team The role is ideal for candidates with a strong background in applied mathematics, systems biology, and computational biology, as well as practical experience in dynamic model development and the analysis of large-scale biological data, who are excited to apply rigorous computational modelling approaches to real biological and biomedical problems. Support and mentorship will be provided to enable strong quantitative researchers to deepen their biological and translational expertise over time. Visit the AU website to learn more about SAiGENCI. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is ideal for someone who thrives in a collaborative and innovative environment with international visibility, and high-impact, conceptually driven cancer research. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: PhD (awarded, or submitted and under examination) in Computational Biology, Systems Biology, Applied Mathematics, Biomedical Engineering, or a closely related quantitative discipline, with demonstrated application to biological systems. Expertise in developing and applying ODE-based models of intracellular signalling, including model formulation, calibration, parameter identifiability, uncertainty and sensitivity analysis. Experience with agent-based or logic-based approaches is advantageous. Demonstrated ability to translate biological and clinical questions into practical computational frameworks, bridge wet- and dry-lab environments, and design model-informed experiments in collaboration with biologists and clinicians. Proven ability to translate complex computational outputs into meaningful biological and clinical insights. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Build on your career with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role a separate document that addresses the selection criteria Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 11 October 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493454) : Evelyn Ruth Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
    },
    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/project-and-governance-lead-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Project and Governance Lead",
      "description": "Project and Governance Lead - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Project and Governance Lead Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 HEO9 Human resources Fixed term - Full-time HEO9 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the People and Culture Pay Accuracy and Entitlements Program Full-time, fixed term contract until 30 September 2028 at the City West campus Salary Range: $135,226 - $144,672 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work  that matters Lead the frameworks that enable successful program delivery. In this influential role, you will champion best-practice governance, reporting, and project management disciplines that underpin one of the University's most significant transformation programs. Partnering with executive leaders, project teams, and stakeholders, you will provide the oversight, coordination, and insights needed to keep the program on track and deliver lasting organisational benefits. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description above  to discover more about this opportunity. The team Join a team delivering meaningful change for our people. The Pay Accuracy and Entitlements Program brings together experts across project management, governance, payroll, compliance, employee relations, change, and education to strengthen payroll practices, enhance compliance, and improve employee outcomes. As the Project and Governance Lead, you will play a pivotal role in bringing these workstreams together, providing program oversight, driving effective governance, and ensuring the successful delivery of key program outcomes. This is a unique opportunity to influence organisational change, work closely with senior leaders, and help shape a program that will have a lasting impact across the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the People and Culture Portfolio. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated experience working in governance, committee or program management office roles within complex programs Proven ability to prepare high-quality written materials for executive audiences, including briefings and reports Proven ability of risk and compliance controls, including payroll or human resources contexts Proven ability to manage documentation with high attention to detail and maintain version control standards Proven ability to manage sensitive information and coordinate governance and reporting activities Demonstrated experience providing secretarial support for Executive Forums, Committees or Boards Experience within large transformation, remediation or regulatory programmes Strong understanding of risk management frameworks Demonstrated experience maintaining decision and action registers Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the  Apply  Now  button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address Submit your application by 11: 30pm Tuesday 22 September 2027 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493496 ): Jessica De Lorenzo Team Lead, Talent Acquisition +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #S-DNI #LI-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) c7ac1104 Last Name (required) 0133c625 Email (required) 963092b6 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) e2903fee Last Name (required) bdaeb785 Email (required) fc134029 Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 5c688200 Last Name (required) dd91b540 Email (required) bd5fbd72 Job Alert 5806afcb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories HEO9 Human resources HEO9 Human resources Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio People and Culture People and Culture Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
