    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/research-officer-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia-0d641d72-42e5-4719-8b84-d1002bba52b2": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training Level B Fixed term - Part-time Level B Add to favourites View favourites Based in the College of Health at the North Adelaide Campus Part-time (0.2 FTE), 24-month fixed-term contract Salary Range: $117,100 – $138,515 pro rata per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Help develop innovative resources addressing climate-related mental health At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Contribute to an innovative research project exploring the mental health impacts of climate-induced heritage loss. You will help develop, deliver and evaluate practical education and professional resources that support more informed and sustainable responses to climate-related distress. The broader project is funded through the MRFF Mental Health and Climate Change initiative and focuses on mitigating the population mental health impacts associated with climate breakdown-related loss or anticipated loss of heritage Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description below to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to Professor Jonathan Jureidini , you will contribute to a multidisciplinary project within the College of Health, supporting research, curriculum development, teaching and the creation of professional education resources. Working alongside the project team and Chief Investigator Associate Professor Toby Freeman , you will contribute to the development of resources designed to improve understanding and responses to climate-related mental health impacts. Visit the AU website to learn more about the College of Health. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role will suit someone who enjoys combining teaching, research and resource development. Working collaboratively while managing a focused portfolio of work, you will have the opportunity to translate research and evidence into practical resources with real-world application. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: A relevant postgraduate qualification and/or equivalent professional experience in a discipline relevant to the project Demonstrated teaching, training or educational experience, including the development or delivery of learning materials Experience undertaking research, literature reviews or desktop research to inform educational or professional resources Demonstrated ability to develop clear and engaging content for different audiences, including training or professional development materials Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with researchers, practitioners and other stakeholders Experience contributing to the evaluation of teaching, training programs or educational resources would be highly regarded Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Monday 21 September 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493435 ): Georgia Borg Talent Acquisition Officer +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au #LI-DNI #S-DNI Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 2ba99208 Last Name (required) 3fa034d6 Email (required) 653c388c Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 141762fa Last Name (required) ce59e40e Email (required) fc06d86f Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 468ff875 Last Name (required) a0982f55 Email (required) 8da31e8e Job Alert 00b3545a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education & Training Level B Education & Training Level B Locations Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Portfolio College of Health College of Health Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details Please choose a portfolio"
