    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-b-school-of-dentistry-adelaide-cbd-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer B (School of Dentistry)",
      "description": "Lecturer B (School of Dentistry) - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Lecturer B (School of Dentistry) Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Level B Fixed term - Full-time Fixed term - Part-time Level B Add to favourites View favourites Based in School of Dentistry at Adelaide City West Campus 2-3 x Level B Part-time/ Full-time Teaching Focused positions (1FTE /0.5FTE), fixed term positions available immediately, Parental leave cover for 12 months Salary Level B ($117,100 - $138,515) per annum (pro-rata if part-time) , plus clinical loading for registered Dentists (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. We are seeking experienced and enthusiastic dental educators to join our team for Semester 2 and make an immediate impact on the education and clinical development of our Bachelor of Dental Surgery (BDS) students. In this role the successful applicant will provide direct clinical supervision for students working in SA Dental Clinics providing dental care to eligible patients, work closely with year coordinators to contribute to assessment and administration and/or coordination of teaching activities. Work that matters This is an exciting opportunity for a dedicated dental professional with APHRA registration to contribute to the next generation of dental practitioners. Based primarily in the Adelaide Health and Medical Sciences building on North Terrace, this opportunity provides essential teaching, teaching administration and clinical supervision across Years 1–5 of the BDS Program, including after-hours clinic supervision and supervision of students on in the Adelaide Dental Hospital or metropolitan clinical sites. Working within a collaborative and supportive environment, as the successful candidate you will be part of various year level teaching teams and will contribute to coordination of teaching activities including management of MyLearning courses; delivery of course content; tutor recruitment and tutor support; setting and marking assessments including written, clinical, viva and OSCE assessments and test invigilation and student support and pastoral care. The team In the School of Dentistry, we value diversity, authenticity, innovation and collaboration. We harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence, providing opportunities to work alongside leading researchers and educators across a broad range of health disciplines. Reporting to the Academic Lead, Student Experience, School of Dentistry, the successful applicant will join a collegial and supportive environment dedicated to excellence in teaching and research, and engagement with community and industry. Visit the School of Dentistry website to learn more. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity, and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation, and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Essential Selection Criteria/Experience: Current Full registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) as a dental practitioner (general dentist) and the ability to meet SA Dental Credentialling which includes a valid Working with Children Check, a National Police Clearance and Healthcare Worker Immunisation Screening Demonstrated skills and experience in the preparation and delivery of high-quality student- centred learning and teaching at an undergraduate level that includes the capacity to incorporate new technologies; as well as assessment activities; and a commitment to excellence in teaching Demonstrated skills and experience in clinical teaching (all aspects of general dentistry), supporting diverse student learners in the clinical environment and commitment to maintaining active contemporary clinical practice and professional activity Demonstrated high level organisational skills, including the ability to prioritise and manage workload within a busy environment and to meet deadlines and work independently and collaboratively in a multi-disciplinary environment Commitment to the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion, and ability to contribute to the diversity of our School community Desirable Criteria/Experience Post-graduate qualifications in higher education/clinical education; Honours; Masters or PhD Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us your suitability for the role a separate document that addresses Selection Criteria Submit your application by 11:30pm Sunday 20 September 2026 Please note that the role description is not attached to this advertisement as it is currently being finalised. For further information about this opportunity, please contact: (quoting reference number 493483) Evelyn Ruth Talent Acquisition Advisor +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. Pursuant to the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (the Act) and the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Regulations 2019 (the Regulations), this position has been deemed prescribed. This role will require the successful candidate to hold a current Working with Children Check. Appointment is subject to a satisfactory National Police Check (NPC) being obtained and maintained. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
