      "title": "Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service",
      "description": "Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Technical Assistant, Hospital and Health Service Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Education & Training HEO3 Continuing - Part-time HEO3 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based within the College of Health, in the Adelaide CBD Part-time (0.4FTE), continuing position (HEO3) $47,006 - $74,733 per annum plus an employer contribution of 17% superannuation applies. At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Help deliver technical services to support simulation and clinical teaching environments, maintain compliance with safety standards and foster a collaborative team culture. Enable high-quality simulation learning in the Horizon Hospital and Health Service by creating realistic props, setting up clinical skills labs and operating audiovisual recording systems. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of Specialist Facilities and Technical Services team within the College of Health Function and is aligned to the Provost Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about the College of Health . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and loves taking on new challenges. You will experience a range of tasks and interactions, giving you the opportunity to use your organisational skills, attention to detail and accuracy, while working collaboratively as part of a team. Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Experience providing technical support in simulation or clinical teaching environments Experience creating and maintaining simulated medical props and moulage Experience operating and maintaining biomedical and audiovisual equipment Experience following laboratory health and safety procedures Experience maintaining consumables and inventory Experience working collaboratively within a team Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Thursday 24 September 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493439): Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. This position is a flexible ordinary hours appointment, which requires ordinary hours to be worked on a rostered shift arrangement that includes performing work both within and outside the span of ordinary hours as specified in the University of South Australia Enterprise Agreement 2023 and its successor enterprise agreements. A flexibility loading will be paid at the appropriate rate for every hour worked outside of the span of ordinary hours as specified in the Enterprise Agreement. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Adelaide University respectfully ackno