    "https://jobs.adelaide.edu.au/jobs/administration-officer-mawson-lakes-sa-australia": {
      "title": "Administration Officer",
      "description": "Administration Officer - Mawson Lakes, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Administration Officer Mawson Lakes, SA, Australia, 5095 Administration HEO4 Fixed term - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in the Future Industries Institute at the Mawson Lakes Campus Full-time, fixed term contract until September 2028 Salary Range starting at $75,366 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) Support a unique joint MSc program with University College London At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters As an Administrative Officer, you will provide a broad range of administrative support to the Future Industries Institute, with a key focus on supporting the UCL Engineering MSc in Global Management of Natural Resources program delivered in partnership with University College London. You will help coordinate the student journey from applications and admissions through to onboarding,  student events and activities, and program completion, while maintaining accurate records, tracking key dates and actions, and ensuring processes progress efficiently. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team Reporting to the Team Lead, Future Industries Institute, you will join a collaborative team of six supporting the Institute’s research, academics, students and international program activity. The team delivers a broad range of administrative services across research, student support, events, communications and day-to-day operations, with responsibilities shared and rotated to provide variety and exposure across the Institute. Visit the AU website to learn more about Future Industries Institute . Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. You will be part of a supportive and collaborative team that values initiative, organisation and a willingness to help one another. This role is well suited to someone who enjoys variety, takes a proactive approach to their work and is comfortable managing detailed administrative processes independently, while working closely with students, professional staff, academics, researchers and external stakeholders. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Post-secondary qualifications or equivalent relevant experience. Experience providing administrative support within a busy, team-based service environment. Strong organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple deadlines, actions and processes accurately. Demonstrated initiative and confidence in independently sourcing information, resolving routine matters and identifying appropriate next steps. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships and provide high-quality service to a diverse range of stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and information systems, particularly spreadsheets, with the ability to quickly learn new systems and processes. Desirable Experience working within a university, higher education or research environment. Experience supporting international student programs, research activities, placements, partnerships or similar initiatives. Experience coordinating complex administrative processes involving multiple stakeholders, competing deadlines and high volumes of correspondence, documentation and data tracking. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm Tuesday 29 September 2026 For further information about this opportunity, please contact (quoting reference number 493482 ): Georgia Borg Talent Acquisition Officer +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Content missing Content missing Recommended Jobs Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Technical Research Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 College Services - Engineering and Information Technology Support automotive safety research through the delivery of technical, laboratory and research activities Knowledge and Compliance Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Advisory and Wellbeing Support compliant pay practices through education, knowledge management and stakeholder engagement, helping drive accuracy, capability and compliance across Adelaide University. Content missing Adelaide University respectfully acknowledges the Kaurna, Boandik and Barngarla First Nations Peoples and their Elders past and present, who are the First Nations’ Traditional Owners of the lands that will be home to our campuses located in Adelaide, Magill, Mawson Lakes, Waite, Roseworthy, Mount Gambier and Whyalla. Disclaimer | Copyright | Privacy | Accessibility | Cookie Preferences Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Tiktok YouTube Weixin Australian University Provider Number PRV14404 | CRICOS Provider Number 04249J Candidate Details"
