      "title": "Academic and Program Services Officer",
      "description": "Academic and Program Services Officer - Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia Manage your settings Search Jobs Visit adelaideuni.edu.au Kiosk mode Together, we will define Adelaide University Together, we will define Adelaide University Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Jobs near me Academic and Program Services Officer Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Administration HEO4 Continuing - Full-time HEO4 Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Based in College of Science located in Adelaide CBD Full-time, Continuing Position Salary Range (HEO 4): $75,366 – $82,607 per annum (plus 17% superannuation) At Adelaide University, we create the opportunities you need to achieve your ambitions – because when you thrive, we thrive. We are transforming education for contemporary learners and global citizens. Building on a proud legacy and shaped by bold ambition, it’s a place of excellence and equity, where our vibrant community of staff are united by our purpose to inspire Australia’s future change-makers and create a better tomorrow. Work that matters Provide administrative support to academic staff and students, supporting quality delivery of coursework programs, courses and related activities. This role encompasses coordinating events, compiling data, and liaising with stakeholders to uphold academic standards and facilitate effective communication within the College. Curious to learn more? Explore the full role description to discover more about this opportunity. The team This role forms part of the Academic and Program Services team within the College and is aligned to the Provost Portfolio within the University. Visit the AU website to learn more about College of Health. Our people Our people are guided by purpose, curiosity and a commitment to lifelong learning. We embrace authenticity, innovation and collaboration, and harness diverse thinking in our pursuit of excellence. This role is perfect for someone who enjoys variety and meeting new people. You will experience a range of tasks and interactions, keeping your workday interesting and engaging. Learn more about our people, what we stand for and what we offer at Careers at AU . Experience To join our community and thrive in this role, you will likely have the following skills and experience: Demonstrated previous experience working in an administrative role in a team-based service environment. Demonstrated written and verbal communication skills including preparation of written materials and experience in liaising with people at all levels both internal and external to an organisation to deliver quality customer service. Demonstrated experience in the interpretation and application of policies and procedures. Demonstrated organisational and time management skills to manage multiple priorities under broad direction. Demonstrated experience in using information systems and the Microsoft Office suite of programs. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity We are committed to fostering a culture of inclusion where diversity is celebrated and everyone feels respected and valued. Adelaide University is an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating a safe, inclusive, and equitable workplace where everyone can thrive. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, and people of all ages, genders, cultural backgrounds, sexual orientations, and gender identities. We are committed to supporting flexible working arrangements and providing reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment process. Launch your future with Adelaide University now. Applying is simple. Simply click on the Apply Now button and upload: your current CV a cover letter that tells us why you’re excited about the role The online application form will list the specific selection criteria that you need to address. Submit your application by 11:30pm, Thursday 1 October 2026 The University reserves the right to close this advertisement before the closing date if a suitable candidate is identified. For further information about this opportunity, please contact ( quoting reference number 493511 ): Georgia Viola Talent Acquisition Adviser +61 8 8302 1700 | careers.adelaideuniversity@adelaide.edu.au Applications welcomed from Australian or NZ citizens, Australian permanent residents and those who have the legal right to work in Australia for the term of appointment. #LI-DNI #S-DNI Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 72911f2e Last Name (required) 5326bfbb Email (required) 075c130a Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Ready to start your application? Apply here. First Name (required) 1978eeae Last Name (required) 0a7f83aa Email (required) c0d0b1ce Apply Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs The Elizabeth Wood Research Fellowship in Musicology Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 The Elizabeth Wood Research Fellowship in Musicology Administration Officer Mawson Lakes, SA, Australia, 5095 Future Industries Institute Provide hands-on administrative support across an international student program, research activities, events and the broader Future Industries Institute. Triage Counsellor Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 Student Success This opportunity forms part of Student Wellbeing and Safety team within the Student Success Function and is aligned to the Student Experience and Success Portfolio within the University. Team Lead, Quality and Compliance Adelaide CBD, SA, Australia, 5000 People Services and Careers Lead a high-performing compliance team to strengthen payroll accuracy, manage audits, mitigate risk and drive continuous improvement across People & Culture. Hear about jobs that are right for you! Sign up to job alerts First Name (required) 1bc1f16d Last Name (required) e919d7e5 Email (required) bc4a76b7 Job Alert bb7bf36d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You c